The DID Document {#chapter-didoc}
=====================================

## Definition ## {#section-didoc-definition}

For every Record, a <dfn>DID Document</dfn> MUST exist. A DID document is a chain of immutable DID document versions (see [DID Document History](#section-didoc-history)). Each version contains the following fields:

<table class="data">
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Field</th><th>Required</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>@context</code></td><td>MUST</td><td>Array of context URIs. MUST start with https://www.w3.org/ns/did/v1. A DID document that contains a Multikey MUST additionally include https://w3id.org/security/multikey/v1</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>id</code></td><td>MUST</td><td>DID of the [=Record=]; identical to the Record DID. MUST NOT change between versions</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>recordEndpoint</code></td><td>MUST</td><td>URL at which the [=Record=] can be retrieved. The <code>recordEndpoint</code> and the <code>id</code> together MUST form the full URL.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>created</code></td><td>MUST</td><td>ISO 8601 timestamp of DID creation. MUST NOT change between versions</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>updated</code></td><td>MUST</td><td>ISO 8601 timestamp of this DID document version. Defines <code>versionTime</code> resolution</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>currentVersionHash</code></td><td>MUST</td><td><code>versionHash</code> of the current finalised [=Record=] version. Omitted if the [=Record=] has no finalised version</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>previousVersionHash</code></td><td>MUST</td><td><code>versionHash</code> of the preceding DID document version. Omitted in the first version</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>proof</code></td><td>MUST (when finalized, unless the schema defines signaturePolicy none)</td><td>One or more Data Integrity proofs over the DID document. See [Proof Procedure](#section-integrity-proof)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>service</code></td><td>MAY</td><td>Array of service entries according to [[DID-CORE]] (<code>id</code>, <code>type</code>, <code>serviceEndpoint</code>) declaring additional, optional access channels (see [Service Entries](#section-didoc-service))</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>controller</code></td><td>MAY</td><td>AgentRecord(s) that control this DID document, per [[DID-CORE]]. Proofs of this DID document are verified against the DID documents of the controllers.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>verificationMethod</code></td><td>MAY</td><td>Per [[DID-CORE]]. Each entry MUST contain `id` (DID URL), `type` Multikey, `controller` (DID of the AgentRecord) and `publicKeyMultibase`. MUST be present for every key used to sign.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>assertionMethod</code></td><td>MAY</td><td>Verification methods allowed for Version proofs (proofPurpose assertionMethod).</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>capabilityInvocation</code></td><td>MAY</td><td>Verification methods allowed for proofs of DID document versions (proofPurpose capabilityInvocation).</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<pre class='example json' title='Record components'>
{
  "@context": [
    "https://www.w3.org/ns/did/v1",
    "https://w3id.org/security/multikey/v1"
  ],
  "id": "did:rwp:d2d14675-50c9-463d-b564-1ea50644c836:a95437ee-25e4-469a-a2e1-c2b250b21e15",
  "recordEndpoint": "https://recordweb.org/resolver/records/",
  "created": "2026-10-26T18:20:00Z",
  "updated": "2026-10-26T18:20:00Z",
  "currentVersionHash": "sha256:474425f9f1f2d1fe78bcec3f41a579c02d5261161c489ab22296980075f37895",
  "proof": [],
  "verificationMethod": [{
    "id": "did:rwp:d2d14675-50c9-463d-b564-1ea50644c836:efd09e7b-5f65-4637-b06c-404a9da97f0b#key-1",
    "type": "Multikey",
    "controller": "did:rwp:d2d14675-50c9-463d-b564-1ea50644c836:efd09e7b-5f65-4637-b06c-404a9da97f0b",
    "publicKeyMultibase": "z6MkpgYzzH9AJJTnsYYMEaaVPZN2t2iCsz76ShftvkBt5jpP"
  }],
  "assertionMethod": [ "did:rwp:d2d14675-50c9-463d-b564-1ea50644c836:a95437ee-25e4-469a-a2e1-c2b250b21e15#key-1" ],
  "capabilityInvocation": [ "did:rwp:d2d14675-50c9-463d-b564-1ea50644c836:a95437ee-25e4-469a-a2e1-c2b250b21e15#key-1" ]
}
</pre>


## History ## {#section-didoc-history}

Every change of a DID document MUST create a new DID document version. A DID document version is immutable once published. Only `id` and `created` MUST NOT change; all other fields MAY change.

A new DID document version MUST be created, and `currentVersionHash` and `updated` MUST be set accordingly, when:

- a [=Record=] version is finalised;
- the storage location (`recordEndpoint`) changes;
- a payload deletion is executed (see [Payload Deletion](#chapter-deletionrecord));
- `service` or `proof` are added, changed or removed.

A new version MUST reference the current latest version as `previousVersionHash`. A [=producer=] or [=custodian=] MUST reject a new version whose `previousVersionHash` is not the `versionHash` of the latest version.


## versionHash ## {#bsection-didoc-versionhash}

The `versionHash` identifies a DID document version and is calculated as follows:

1. Serialise the DID document fields `@context`, `id`, `controller`, `recordEndpoint`, `service`, `verificationMethod`, `assertionMethod`, `capabilityInvocation`, `created`, `updated`, `currentVersionHash`, `previousVersionHash`, and `proof` as canonical JSON ([[RFC8785]]). Fields not present are omitted.
2. Calculate SHA-256 over the result.
3. Encode the digest as `sha256:` followed by 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters.

<pre class='example code' title='versionHash calculation'>
versionHash = "sha256:" + hex( SHA-256( canonicalize({@context, id, [controller], recordEndpoint, [service,] [verificationMethod,] [assertionMethod,] [capabilityInvocation,] created, updated, [currentVersionHash], [previousVersionHash], [proof]}) ) )
</pre>

Fields not present are omitted.


## History Verification ## {#section-didoc-verification}

A verifier checking a DID document version MUST:

1. recompute the `versionHash`;
2. check that `previousVersionHash` equals the `versionHash` of the predecessor;
3. verify at least one `proof` as defined in [Proof Procedure](#section-integrity-proof);
4. check that `updated` is later than `updated` of the predecessor.

The verification method of a proof MUST be listed in capabilityInvocation of
(a) the preceding DID document version, if the DID document belongs to an AgentRecord. For the first version it is the version itself.
(b) the current DID document of one of its controllers, for any other DID document.


## Service Entries ## {#section-didoc-service}

A DID document MAY contain a `service` property. Each entry MUST follow the structure defined for `service` in [[DID-CORE]] and MUST have `id`, `type` and `serviceEndpoint`.

The `recordEndpoint` remains the only mandatory access channel. An implementation is not required to offer any `service` entry.

A `service` entry is a declaration of availability. It is not a grant of access. Authorisation for using a declared service MUST remain subject to the applicable access policy (see [Access Control](#chapter-access-control)).

This specification defines the following `type` values:

<table class="data">
  <thead><tr><th>type</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>RWPPublicRecordAccess</code></td><td>Endpoint returning a restricted or public view of the [=Record=] for requesters without full access rights</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RWPRecordReferrers</code></td><td>Endpoint returning all finalised `RelationRecords` ([=CaseRecord=] and [=AssertionRecord=]) referring to this [=Record=] within the same namespace. The response contains a list of records each with a list of finalised versions</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>RWPFunctionRegistry</code></td><td>Endpoint returning a machine-readable list of the functions supported for the [=Record=], derived from the `capabilities` of its [=SchemaRecord=] (see [SchemaRecord](#chapter-schemarecord))</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

Other `type` values, including protocol-specific ones (for example `DIDCommMessaging` or an MCP-based channel), MAY be used. Their semantics are defined by their respective specifications and are outside the scope of RWP.

A DID document MUST NOT be treated as immutable in the sense of a fixed resolution result, since a new version MAY be created at any time. A specific version, identified by `versionHash`, is immutable.


## Resolver Requirements ## {#section-didoc-resolver}

An implementation claiming the [=resolver=] role MUST provide a DID resolver that:

- Resolves DIDs of the method `rwp` and returns the associated DID document
- Delivers the DID document as JSON-LD in accordance with [[DID-CORE]]
- Where the DID document contains a `service` property, delivers it as part of the DID document.
- Supports the resolver options `versionHash` and `versionTime`
- Returns HTTP 200 when the DID is known
- Returns HTTP 400 when both `versionHash` and `versionTime` are given
- Returns HTTP 403 where the resolver's applicable access policy does not permit the requester to obtain the DID document
- Returns HTTP 404 when the DID is unknown, when `versionHash` is unknown, or when `versionTime` is earlier than `created`
- Returns HTTP 410 when the DID is known but the [=Record=] has been deleted completely (see [Deletion](#section-deletionrecord-regimes)). Payload deletion does NOT result in 410
- Retains every DID document version for as long as the DID is resolvable. Payload deletion does not remove the history

`versionHash` and `versionTime` are mutually exclusive. Without either, the [=resolver=] MUST return the latest version. With `versionHash`, it MUST return exactly that version. With `versionTime`, it MUST return the version with the greatest `updated` less than or equal to the given time.

An implementation claiming another RWP profile or role MAY rely on a [=resolver=] operated by another conformant implementation. It is not required to operate a DID resolver itself unless it claims the [=resolver=] role.

A [=producer=] or [=custodian=] that creates or manages RWP Records MUST ensure that the associated Record DIDs remain resolvable in accordance with this specification.

